# Vendored unified-diff patch files legitimately contain single-space blank
# context lines (the unified-diff format requires a leading space on every
# context line, so a blank context line is exactly one space). git's whitespace
# checker (`git diff --check` / `git show --check`, run by the build-image CI
# gate) misreads those as trailing-whitespace defects because the tracked file
# is itself a diff. Disable whitespace checking for the patch collections so the
# gate passes. This does NOT weaken setup.sh's `git diff --check`, which runs
# against the *applied* SGLang source tree, not against these patch blobs.
patches/**       -whitespace
llmcompressor-patches/**  -whitespace
ream-patches/**  -whitespace
benchmarks/profiling/**/*.patch.txt  -whitespace
